# Provenance of schema/schema.graphql (hadron-cli#2043, retire with #2658).
#
# The snapshot is NOT an export of a commit on hadron-server main. It is the
# export of the merge of these two named hadron-server commits, because the
# CLI needs hadron-server#4219 (the S4+S6 renames) and #4414
# (workedFromRoleTaskRefs) but cannot yet regenerate against S2 (#4513, which
# removed fields the old-shape decision.graphql selects).
#
# scripts/pin-server-sdl.sh reproduces that merge byte-deterministically, and
# its --verify checks the export against merge_sha/sdl_sha256/sdl_lines below
# and against the committed snapshot. The nightly schema-drift job checks the
# pin the same way (its pin-verify job); the drift job proper does something
# else: it compares the snapshot against hadron-server main, which the pin
# deliberately differs from until #2658 retires it.
#
# head= is the commit merged INTO base= (the merge's second parent), not the
# resulting merge commit — whose SHA the script reproduces deterministically
# and records as merge_sha=.
#
# sdl_sha256/sdl_lines were produced with the tool versions recorded below as
# tsx= and graphql= — the single place they live: scripts/pin-server-sdl.sh
# reads them here, and the schema-drift job's SDL_EXPORT interpolates the same
# keys (a graphql minor can change printSchema bytes, so a silent float trips
# the sha for a non-pin reason). Bump deliberately, then re-run --verify.
base=2d1cd5c669be735eeeecf44941d86ad3f4f7688f
head=47b0672fb5270123bd2d4c49a9b5365106cb3b22
merge_sha=3dedeab1783ea6554145c693fd70b7c5b24e9236
# overlay= (cli#2727, retire with #2658): a unified diff applied to the export
# of the merge above. It adds GrantSigningRequest.lastRefusedAt, byte-identical
# to hadron-server c9d7820e (#4581) typeDefs; that commit sits after S2 (#4513),
# so it cannot be merged into this pin. pre_overlay_sdl_sha256 is the export
# before the overlay (the old sdl_sha256), sdl_sha256/sdl_lines are after it.
# A second overlay (cli#2677, retire with #2658) adds WorkerTerminalReason
# multiple_terminals and no_screen, byte-identical to hadron-server 6a22634c
# (#4566, closes #4558); it too sits after S2. overlay= may repeat: the patches
# apply in the order listed, and the sha/lines below are after all of them.
overlay=schema/overlay/4581-lastRefusedAt.patch
overlay=schema/overlay/4566-terminal-reasons.patch
pre_overlay_sdl_sha256=67c6459430ade0373dfac3864a4ea8fe2d1c2e73044d679b40f29d777385b7c1
sdl_lines=22725
sdl_sha256=19c4be4b85b2692c473f3ce4dcb683628dfc8c799812648a620ab772ce04788a
